# Packages Huginn OS has its own app for. If a dependency ever pulls one in, the build takes it out again
# (and stops if that would take anything we asked for with it).
ark
dolphin
gwenview
kate
kde-spectacle
konsole
okular
systemsettings
calamares
polkit-kde-agent-1
sddm-theme-breeze
# Huginn signs you in itself (apps/huginn_signind.py)
sddm
plymouth-theme-spinner
# Plasma's background services: Huginn's session daemon does their work (notifications, power and idle, keys and
# levels, Wi‑Fi secrets, Bluetooth pairing)
plasma-nm
plasma-pa
powerdevil
bluedevil
# KWin and Plasma's workspace: Huginn's own compositor draws the desktop and the sign-in screen
kwin-wayland
kwin-x11
kwin-common
plasma-workspace
plasma-session-wayland
kscreen
# Papirus: replaced by Huginn's own icon theme (2026-11-19)
papirus-icon-theme
# KDE's desktop portal and its integration for Qt apps: Huginn's portal and GTK's answer apps, and Huginn's own Qt
# look carries Huginn's look and Open and Save windows to Qt apps (2026-11-27)
xdg-desktop-portal-kde
plasma-integration
kde-cli-tools
kio-extras
kde-config-gtk-style
# KDE's Breeze style for Qt and for GTK, and what came with it: Huginn's own Qt look and GTK 3 theme do their work
# (Breeze's icons and pointers stay: 20-desktop.list) (2026-11-27)
breeze
breeze-gtk-theme
kde-style-breeze
kde-style-breeze-data
kwin-style-breeze
breeze-wallpaper
# KDE Connect: Phone has its own link now (apps/huginn_phoned.py, KDE Connect's protocol), and the desktop theme it
# brought along (2026-11-27)
kdeconnect
plasma-desktoptheme
# KDE's RDP server: Screen Sharing is the compositor's own now (compositor/src/rdp.rs) (2026-11-27)
krdp
# qt6ct and Kvantum: Huginn's own Qt look (qt/: a platform theme and a widget style) does their work, and puts Qt
# apps' menu bars in the top bar (2026-11-27)
qt6ct
qt6-style-kvantum
qt6-style-kvantum-l10n
qt6-style-kvantum-themes
qt-style-kvantum-themes
# The last of KDE: layer-shell-qt (Huginn's own module makes the shell's windows: qt/layershell), the QML modules for
# NetworkManager and BlueZ (the shell asks them itself), and KConfig's command-line tools (Settings writes its files
# itself) (2026-11-27)
layer-shell-qt
liblayershellqtinterface6
qml6-module-org-kde-layershell
qml6-module-org-kde-networkmanager
libkf6networkmanagerqt6
qml6-module-org-kde-bluezqt
libkf6bluezqt6
libkf6bluezqt-data
libkf6config-bin
# KDE's pointers: Huginn draws its own (pointers/make_pointers.py); Adwaita's and DMZ's stay to choose from (2026-11-28)
breeze-cursor-theme
oxygen-cursor-theme
# Breeze's icons: Huginn's icon theme answers every standard name itself now (scripts/icon_names.py), so nothing of
# KDE's is left, artwork included (2026-11-28)
breeze-icon-theme
kf6-breeze-icon-theme
